sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The universality of rule 110, one of the simplest possible cellular automaton rules, implies that universality is far more common than previously thought and should occur in a very wide range of systems, including many with rather simple rules.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Universality should be common, including among very simple rules";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “The Significance of Universality in Rule 110” (from p. 690), p. 690. Scope: simple programs of all kinds"
}
